From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:52:21 -0400
Subject: feat: quieter by default, and the updater looks at launch and every
 six hours

The owner's choices of 2026-10-21 after 0.3.0 beta 1, in one patch because
they share the preferences, Settings' Stedding page and the updater:

- Hints off by default, each with a switch in Settings > Stedding: the toast
  offering Undo after a close (tabs R30, settings T17), the routed "Opened in
  <Space> - Undo" notice (routing D4, "Show notices about Spaces"), and the
  note on how to leave a full screen the person started (toolbar T45, "Show
  how to leave full screen"); a page's own full screen keeps Chromium's note,
  which guards against a page drawing a fake browser. The warning that pinning
  a tab out of a Space with an Independent session signs it out stays on, with
  a switch of its own (sessions S33, "Warn when pinning signs a tab out").
- The updater checks at a launch when the last check is over an hour old,
  and every six hours while the browser runs, on the Mac through Sparkle's
  schedule and a background check at launch, on Windows through its own
  schedule (updates Up1, Up6, Up7, Up14, Up20). A copy that checked in the
  morning had not been offered an evening's release until the next day. On
  Windows a download that fails tries again within the hour, as a feed that
  cannot be reached does, and the installer is downloaded at LOW priority, not
  IDLE (BACKLOG S-279): at IDLE SimpleURLLoader writes the file on a
  BEST_EFFORT sequence, which starved while a UI Automation client read the
  window; the body stopped being read after the stream's first 6 MB, GitHub
  reset the stalled stream after three minutes, and the copy waited six hours.

Tests: UndoCloseByDefaultTest, IsolationMarkTest's two notice tests,
FullscreenHintTest (a person's full screen and a page's), AppUpdaterMacTest
and WinAppUpdaterTest's schedule tests (AFailedDownloadTriesAgainWithinTheHour
and TheInstallerDownloadIsNotLeftToIdleTime among them); each fails without its change, and the
toast tests turn their switch on.

Why: the owner found the hints in the way and the release late to arrive.
Removable when: never as a whole; the next re-cut gives each part a patch of
its own (patches/README.md).
